  <running_head>Epist. 10. ad</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>uni</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Magistratum atque in ejusmodi censu-</l>
    <l n="2">ris, canonibus decretis ferendis &amp; im-</l>
    <l n="3">perandis, summum &amp; ultimum judi-</l>
    <l n="4">cium summamque authoritatem per-</l>
    <l n="5">tinere ad Magistratum, non vero ad</l>
    <l n="6">Synodos aut Pastores.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">3. Cum ergo canones, decreta, censurae</l>
    <l n="8">latae à pastoribus, definitiones &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">constitutiones nullam vim legis habe-</l>
    <l n="10">ant, quae parendi illis cuiquam neces-</l>
    <l n="11">sitatem imponant, citra sanctionem,</l>
    <l n="12">voluntatem &amp; approbationem Magi-</l>
    <l n="13">stratus, plane conficitur eum teneri</l>
    <l n="14">&amp; obligari, vel illas constitutiones &amp;</l>
    <l n="15">definitiones pastorales aut synodales</l>
    <l n="16">caeco judicio approbare &amp; ratas habere</l>
    <l n="17">citra examen proprii judicii suggeren-</l>
    <l n="18">tis, quod concordent cum sacra scrip-</l>
    <l n="19">tura, aut ab ea discordent: quodque</l>
    <l n="20">plus minusve cedant in bonum Ecclesiae:</l>
    <l n="21">vel illas constitutiones Ecclesi-</l>
    <l n="22">asticas in totum, saltem de illis tantum</l>
    <l n="23">suo assensu ratum habere, quantum</l>
    <l n="24">post examen debitum proprii judicii,</l>
    <l n="25">ipsi videbitur bonum, justum &amp;</l>
    <l n="26">aequum. Hic, inquit Maccovius, con-</l>
    <l n="27">strictos teneo vindices potestatis Eccle-</l>
    <l n="28">siasticae &amp; compello ad assentiendum</l>
    <l n="29">uni</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "uni" is at the right foot; the running head is the title repeated at top. Text is of a single column with no marginal notes. Some words are slightly blurred (e.g. "Ecclesiasticae") but were read with reasonable confidence.</notes>
